sequenceDiagram
    participant User as User / Dashboard
    participant K8sAPI as Kubernetes API Server<br/>443/TCP HTTPS TLS
    participant Webhook as Training Operator Webhook<br/>9443/TCP HTTPS TLS
    participant Controller as Training Operator Controller
    participant Kubelet as Kubelet<br/>10250/TCP HTTPS mTLS
    participant Pods as Training Pods<br/>(replicas)
    participant HeadlessSvc as Headless Services<br/>Dynamic/TCP
    participant Volcano as Volcano / scheduler-plugins<br/>443/TCP HTTPS TLS

    Note over User,HeadlessSvc: Flow 1: Training Job Lifecycle

    User->>K8sAPI: POST {Job}CR (e.g. PyTorchJob)<br/>Auth: Bearer token / OIDC
    K8sAPI->>Webhook: POST /validate-kubeflow-org-v1-*<br/>HTTPS/9443, TLS<br/>Auth: Kubernetes API token
    Webhook-->>K8sAPI: Admission Response (allow/deny)
    K8sAPI-->>User: CR created

    Controller->>K8sAPI: Watch {Job} CRDs<br/>HTTPS/443, TLS<br/>Auth: ServiceAccount token
    K8sAPI-->>Controller: Job event (ADDED/MODIFIED)

    Controller->>K8sAPI: Create Pods + Headless Services<br/>HTTPS/443, TLS<br/>Auth: ServiceAccount token
    K8sAPI->>Kubelet: Schedule pod creation<br/>HTTPS/10250, mTLS<br/>Auth: Client cert
    Kubelet-->>Pods: Pods running

    Pods->>HeadlessSvc: Inter-replica communication<br/>Dynamic/TCP, No encryption<br/>DNS-based discovery

    Controller->>K8sAPI: Update Job status<br/>HTTPS/443, TLS

    Note over Controller,Volcano: Flow 2: Gang Scheduling (Optional)

    Controller->>K8sAPI: Create PodGroup CR<br/>HTTPS/443, TLS<br/>Auth: ServiceAccount token
    K8sAPI-->>Volcano: PodGroup event
    Volcano->>K8sAPI: Schedule pods together<br/>HTTPS/443, TLS<br/>Auth: ServiceAccount token

    Note over Controller,Pods: Flow 3: MPI Job Execution

    Controller->>K8sAPI: Create SA, Role, RoleBinding,<br/>ConfigMap for launcher<br/>HTTPS/443, TLS
    K8sAPI-->>Controller: Resources created

    Controller->>K8sAPI: Create Launcher + Worker pods<br/>HTTPS/443, TLS
    K8sAPI->>Kubelet: Schedule pods

    Note right of Pods: Launcher pod uses kubectl exec<br/>to run commands on workers<br/>via per-job ServiceAccount

    Pods->>K8sAPI: kubectl exec (pods/exec)<br/>HTTPS/443, TLS<br/>Auth: Per-job SA token
    K8sAPI->>Pods: Exec into worker pods<br/>HTTPS/10250, mTLS

    Pods->>Pods: MPI processes communicate<br/>Dynamic/TCP, No encryption<br/>OMPI RSH agent
